#NEXUS

[ fanti2015a_fig23: S-DIVA biogeography tree (Bayesian topology) with pie-chart nodes and a dispersal/vicariance curve above a stage timescale; 29 tips. Katepensaurus, Nigersaurus and the Demandasaurus clade sit on one vertical carrying two stacked pies: read as (Katepensaurus,(Nigersaurus,(Demandasaurus,(Rebbachisaurus,Tataouinea)))), two nodes at zero length. Topology transcribed from the figure and checked node by node (2026-10-29); topology only. ]

